  "synopsis": {
    "value": "Tous Les Jours is a french-asian bakery-café brand. Its ownership maps to CJ Foodville / CJ Group. Canonical pack: 150 units; 3 company-owned / 147 franchisee-owned. The canonical estate mixes company and franchise restaurants, so corporate can validate technology directly while systemwide deployment must also work economically for franchisees. For RBB, the ownership hierarchy should shape account strategy: determine whether technology, payments and procurement decisions sit at brand corporate, a parent platform or the operator level. Priority lenses are POS/payments, digital guest experience, labor impact, operational throughput, reliability and measurable restaurant-level ROI appropriate to the concept.",
